.IX Title "Lucy::Search::Collector 3pm"
.TH Lucy::Search::Collector 3pm 2026-09-16 "perl v5.40.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
Lucy::Search::Collector \- Process hits.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&    # Abstract base class.
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
A Collector decides what to do with the hits that a
Matcher iterates through, based on how the
abstract \fBcollect()\fR method is implemented.
.PP
Collectors operate on individual segments, but must operate within the
context of a larger collection.  Each time the collector moves to a new
segment, \fBSet_Reader()\fR, \fBSet_Base()\fR and \fBSet_Matcher()\fR will be called, and the
collector must take the updated information into account.
.SH CONSTRUCTORS
.IX Header "CONSTRUCTORS"
.SS new
.IX Subsection "new"
.Vb 9
\&    package MyCollector;
\&    use base qw( Lucy::Search::Collector );
\&    our %foo;
\&    sub new {
\&        my $self = shift\->SUPER::new;
\&        my %args = @_;
\&        $foo{$$self} = $args{foo};
\&        return $self;
\&    }
.Ve
.PP
Abstract constructor.  Takes no arguments.
.SH "ABSTRACT METHODS"
.IX Header "ABSTRACT METHODS"
.SS collect
.IX Subsection "collect"
.Vb 1
\&    $collector\->collect($doc_id);
.Ve
.PP
Do something with a doc id.  (For instance, keep track of the docs
with the ten highest scores.)
.IP \(bu 4
\&\fBdoc_id\fR \- A segment document id.
.SH INHERITANCE
.IX Header "INHERITANCE"
Lucy::Search::Collector isa Clownfish::Obj.
